      "writtenOn": "2026-06-05T19:34:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That error is surprising because Bazel’s `java_library` supports both `exports` and `neverlink`.\n\nSo my first suspicion is that your local build is not resolving `java_library` to the expected rule, or that some external repo/module is stale or locally overridden.\n\nCould you try:\n\n```bash\nbazel clean --expunge\nbazel mod graph | grep -E \"bazlets|rules_java|rules_jvm_external\"\ngrep -R \"override_module\\|override_repository\\|local_path_override\\|git_override\" .bazelrc* MODULE.bazel 2\u003e/dev/null\n```\n\nCI being green suggests this may be local state or a local override rather than the change itself.",
      "parentUuid": "a2d13844_b9a027d7",
      "revId": "646b3735965fc44b816109722e6b986067c4c3aa",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
